Fixed Rivet’s still-card slide. All 18 arsenal weapons and wheel slot 0 now walk and run at both art pitches. The five weapons with drawn armed grids matched the baseline byte for byte across all **1,440 comparison frames**.

| Wheel selection | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Hands, slot 0 | Already stepped | Same empty-claw gait |
| Pistol | Already stepped | Same painted pistol gait |
| Gloria, rocket launcher, assault rifle, chainsaw, electro baton | Boots stayed fixed while the ground moved | Boots alternate and the selected weapon follows the claw |

I chose **option (b)**. Masking the donor pistol exposed the floor through Rivet’s wrist and torso. The bare-claw grid lets the actual held part follow the painted palm. At 64 px/m, the repaired carries averaged **1.1 cm** of net stance drift walking and **5.3 cm** running. The underlying run still holds some drawings for 13–14 ticks, so some sliding remains visible within a step.

[Before film](C:/Users/kazda/kiro/gtai-masters/n24/motion/before/legs_32.mp4) · [After film](C:/Users/kazda/kiro/gtai-masters/n24/motion/after/legs_32.mp4) · [22 matched comparisons](C:/Users/kazda/kiro/gtai-masters/n24/motion/) · [Per-weapon measurements](C:/Users/kazda/kiro/gtai-wt/n23-controls/evidence/n24-motion/slide_after.md). Both films were verified at 1080p60, 26.4 seconds.

